<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $295 mln Oct 9.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $295 mln Oct 9.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $295 million surplus on October 9 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 9</p>
<p>Exports: $217.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $170.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $354.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $106.4 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $295 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.167 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $945 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.733 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $910 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.045 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
